## 
## BLACKLISTED APPLICATIONS (APP BLACKLISTER)
## 

# This is the list that the App Blacklister module reads and applies.
# Usage:
# Write down the package IDs of apps that you want to blacklist, without any additions.
#   Eg. "com.example.example_app"
# Adding spaces and/or unnecessary characters will most likely result w/ the rule not working. You can do comments though.
#   Eg. "com.example.example_app " will not work, neither will "com.example.example_app;", "# com.example.example_app" is just a comment.
# You can add wildcards to either the left, the right or to any place if you want to blacklist a whole pattern rather than just one package.
#   Eg. "com.google.*" to do a FULLY HARDCORE de-Google (btw NEVER do that on any ROM that uses the Google Mainline components)

# Default rule: Android Developer Verifier
com.google.android.verifier

# Default rule: ironSource's ad service packages AppCloud (which is usually seen in some Samsung and Motorola devices) and AppServices (which is usually seen in some Nothing devices)
#   (also a showcase for the wildcard pattern function)
com.aura.oobe.*

# Do YOUR magic of wiping FSA bloatware.
